1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means the EcoKnowGames Creator tool, including all source
code, runtime scripts, and associated assets contained in this
repository.

1.2 "Generated Work" means any game, application, or interactive
experience created, compiled, or exported using the Software, including
any work that bundles, incorporates, or depends upon the Software's
runtime scripts.

1.3 "Research Purpose" means non-commercial academic research, data
collection, policy development, environmental assessment, public
education, or any related activity conducted for the public benefit
without expectation of commercial gain.

1.4 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software or a Generated Work
for product development, retail sale, licensing, corporate grant
applications, or any other activity from which financial profit or
commercial advantage is sought, directly or indirectly.

1.5 "Publicly Distribute" means making the Software or a Generated Work
available to any person or entity beyond the user's own organisation or
immediate research collaborators, whether by sale, gift, download,
broadcast, or any other means.


2. COPYRIGHT

The Software is copyright (c) 2026 University of Stirling. All rights
reserved. The University of Stirling is the sole copyright holder of the
